## Making File System Statics Testable

The best approach is to adopt the **`System.IO.Abstractions`** NuGet package — it's a battle-tested library that wraps the entire `System.IO` surface behind mockable interfaces.

### 1. Install the package

```bash
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

### 2. Register in DI

```csharp
// In Program.cs or Startup.cs:
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

### 3. Inject `IFileSystem` into your classes

```csharp
public class MyService(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string Load(string path)
        => fileSystem.File.ReadAllText(path);

    public void Save(string path, string content)
        => fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(path, content);

    public bool EnsureDirectory(string path)
        => fileSystem.Directory.Exists(path);
}
```

### 4. Test with `MockFileSystem`

```bash
dotnet add <YourTestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```

```csharp
[Test]
public void Load_ReturnsFileContent()
{
    var mockFs = new MockFileSystem(new Dictionary<string, MockFileData>
    {
        { "/data/config.json", new MockFileData("{\"key\": \"value\"}") }
    });

    var service = new MyService(mockFs);

    Assert.Equal("{\"key\": \"value\"}", service.Load("/data/config.json"));
}

[Test]
public void Save_WritesFile()
{
    var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
    mockFs.Directory.CreateDirectory("/output");

    var service = new MyService(mockFs);
    service.Save("/output/result.txt", "hello");

    Assert.Equal("hello", mockFs.File.ReadAllText("/output/result.txt"));
}

[Test]
public void EnsureDirectory_ReturnsFalse_WhenMissing()
{
    var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
    var service = new MyService(mockFs);

    Assert.False(service.EnsureDirectory("/nonexistent"));
}
```

### Why this over a custom wrapper?

| Consideration | `System.IO.Abstractions` | Custom `IFileService` |
|---|---|---|
| Coverage | Entire `System.IO` surface | Only what you wrap today |
| Maintenance | Community-maintained | You maintain it |
| Test helpers | `MockFileSystem` included | You build your own mocks |
| Adoption cost | One NuGet + replace `File.` → `fileSystem.File.` | Same |

---

**Next step:** Once you've added the package and injected `IFileSystem`, you can mechanically replace all `File.*` / `Directory.*` call sites. Let me know if you'd like help migrating the actual call sites in your code.
